app: "Bad" must be lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, up to 40 characters
workloads.job.schedule: expected exactly 5 fields, found 1: [never]
workloads.job: a cron workload has no routes or port
workloads.job.timeout: "forever" isn't a duration such as 30m
workloads.job.ports: only web and worker workloads publish ports
workloads.rel: a release workload runs once per deploy; it has no routes, port or schedule
workloads.site: a static workload needs dir, the directory to serve
workloads.site: a static workload has dir only, no image, build or port
workloads.site.routes[0].port: a static workload serves on its own port only
workloads.web: give either image or build
workloads.web: dir is for static workloads
workloads.web: order is for release workloads
workloads.web.grace: "20m" must be a duration from 1s to 10m
workloads.web.resources.pids: must be 16 or more
workloads.web.ports: a workload that publishes a port must be singleton: true, so the old container lets go of the port before the new one takes it
workloads.web.ports[0].port: must be a port number, 1 to 65535
workloads.web.ports[0].host_port: must be a port number, 1 to 65535
workloads.web.ports[0].protocol: "sctp" isn't tcp or udp
workloads.web.ports[0].address: "nowhere" isn't an IP address; leave it out to listen on every one
workloads.web.ports[1]: 443 on the machine belongs to the edge
workloads.web.ports[2]: 3478/tcp is already published by job
workloads.web.aliases: "Bad" must be lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
workloads.web.health: give a path or a command, not both
workloads.web.health.command: an argument is empty
workloads.web.health.timeout: "soon" isn't a duration such as 90s
workloads.web.mounts[0]: volume "nowhere" isn't declared under data.volumes
workloads.web.mounts[0]: path must be absolute
workloads.web: a web workload needs port, the container port it listens on
workloads.web.routes[0]: host "not a host" isn't a hostname
workloads.web.routes[0]: path "nope" must start with / and is a prefix, without wildcards
workloads.web.routes[0].dns: "sideways" isn't direct or proxied
workloads.web.routes[0].auth: "magic" isn't loom
workloads.web.routes[0].origin_pull: "strict" isn't optional or required
workloads.web.routes[0].port: must be a port number
workloads.web.routes[2]: a.com / is already routed to web
workloads.web.routes[2].origin_pull: needs dns: proxied, since only Cloudflare's proxy presents the client certificate; set dns: proxied or leave origin_pull out
workloads.web.user: "Nope!" must be a user, uid, or user:group
workloads.web.capabilities: "bad cap" isn't a capability name such as NET_BIND_SERVICE
workloads.web.tmpfs: "relative" must be an absolute path
workloads.web.env: "bad" must be an UPPER_CASE name
workloads.web: KEY is both a secret and a plain env value
workloads.web.secrets: "lower" must be an UPPER_CASE name
workloads.web.resources.memory: "lots" must look like 512m or 2g
workloads.web.resources.cpus: must be 0 to 64
workloads.web.health.path: must start with /
workloads.what: kind "blob" isn't one of web, static, worker, cron, release
routes: a.com has dns "" on one route and "direct" on another; use one
routes: a.com has origin_pull "" on one route and "required" on another; give every route to a.com the same origin_pull
data.volumes: "Bad" must be lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
data.volumes: "postgres" is helios's own volume for the database; pick another name
data.postgres.version: "9" isn't a supported major version (15 to 18)
data.postgres.user: "Bad User" must be lowercase letters, digits and underscores
data.postgres.init: must be inside the source
data.postgres.env: "bad" must be an UPPER_CASE name
data.postgres.secrets: "lower" must be an UPPER_CASE name
secrets.generate.BOTH: "nope" must be hex:N, base64:N, base64url:N or value:TEXT
secrets: BOTH is both generated and derived
secrets.generate: "lower" must be an UPPER_CASE name
secrets.generate.lower: hex: wants 8 to 256 random bytes, not "1"
secrets.derive.BOTH: has an unmatched { or }
